{"id":"portswigger-web-security-academy--server-side-vulnerabilities--file-upload-vulnerabilities--web-shell-upload-via-content-type-restriction-bypass","path":"portswigger-web-security-academy/server-side-vulnerabilities/file-upload-vulnerabilities/web-shell-upload-via-content-type-restriction-bypass.md","title":"Web shell upload via Content-Type restriction bypass","category":"portswigger-web-security-academy","source":"https://github.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/blob/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/portswigger-web-security-academy/server-side-vulnerabilities/file-upload-vulnerabilities/web-shell-upload-via-content-type-restriction-bypass.md","html":"<h1 id=\"web-shell-upload-via-content-type-restriction-bypass\">Web shell upload via Content-Type restriction bypass</h1>\n<h2 id=\"description\">Description</h2>\n<p>This lab contains a vulnerable image upload function. It attempts to prevent users from uploading unexpected file types, but relies on checking user-controllable input to verify this.</p>\n<p>To solve the lab, upload a basic PHP web shell and use it to exfiltrate the contents of the file <code>/home/carlos/secret</code>. Submit this secret using the button provided in the lab banner.</p>\n<p>You can log in to your own account using the following credentials: <code>wiener:peter</code></p>\n<h2 id=\"solution\">Solution</h2>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand Web shell upload via Content-Type restriction bypass screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(111).png\" alt=\"Web shell upload via Content-Type restriction bypass screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>After login as Wiener user there's an upload option to upload avatar image:</p>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand Web shell upload via Content-Type restriction bypass screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(112).png\" alt=\"Web shell upload via Content-Type restriction bypass screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>with the avatar image at this path/location:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://0a890067048524a181330c1d0073004e.web-security-academy.net/my-account?id=wiener\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://0a890067048524a181330c1d0073004e.web-security-academy.net</a><a href=\"https://0ab300990381641d80b5b7de005e0030.web-security-academy.net/resources/images/avatarDefault.svg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">/resources/images/avatarDefault.svg</a></p>\n<p>We need to obtain Carlos's secret, we can do it upload a php shell (<code>php_web_shell.php</code>) that get secret file content</p>\n<div class=\"walkthrough-command\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-command\">Copy command</button><pre><code class=\"language-php\">&lt;?php echo file_get_contents('/home/carlos/secret'); ?&gt;\n</code></pre></div>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand Web shell upload via Content-Type restriction bypass screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(113).png\" alt=\"Web shell upload via Content-Type restriction bypass screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>there's a filtering and we can't upload php shell, seeing the output message file types allowed are: image/jpeg and image/png, so we can use the Burp Repeater to modify request updating Content-Type</p>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand Web shell upload via Content-Type restriction bypass screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(99).png\" alt=\"Web shell upload via Content-Type restriction bypass screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>Infact, inserting: image/jpeg we're able to upload our php web shell bypassing controls:</p>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand Web shell upload via Content-Type restriction bypass screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(100).png\" alt=\"Web shell upload via Content-Type restriction bypass screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>We know the file location and we can open it going to: <a href=\"https://0a890067048524a181330c1d0073004e.web-security-academy.net/my-account?id=wiener\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://0a890067048524a181330c1d0073004e.web-security-academy.net</a><a href=\"https://0ab300990381641d80b5b7de005e0030.web-security-academy.net/files/avatars/php_web_shell.php\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">/files/avatars/php_web_shell.php</a></p>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand Web shell upload via Content-Type restriction bypass screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(101).png\" alt=\"Web shell upload via Content-Type restriction bypass screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Carlos's Secret</summary>\n\n<p>FYw9wjdc53Z6eePuSDiWMPkmrVT6kzvF</p>\n</details>\n\n<p>Obtaining Carlos's secret and solving the lab.</p>\n<figure><button type=\"button\" class=\"image-expand\" aria-label=\"Expand Web shell upload via Content-Type restriction bypass screenshot\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Perryong/Writeups-and-Walkthroughs/dd03effbc624dbb8789fbd7775369769cec81a36/.gitbook/assets/image%20(102).png\" alt=\"Web shell upload via Content-Type restriction bypass screenshot\"></button><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n","toc":[{"id":"description","title":"Description","level":2},{"id":"solution","title":"Solution","level":2}],"excerpt":"Web shell upload via Content-Type restriction bypass Description This lab contains a vulnerable image upload function. It attempts to prevent users from uploading unexpected file types, but relies on checking user-contro","searchText":"Description Solution"}